  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are playing a computer game. In the current level of the game, you have to fight NNN monsters.\n\nThe monsters will appear in order from 111 to NNN, that is, the ithi^{th}ith monster will appear after the (i−1)th(i-1)^{th}(i−1)th monster.\n\nAs soon as a monster appears:\n\n\nYou must fight with the newly appeared monster, leaving aside any other monster you were fighting with.\nIf you manage to kill the monster you are fighting with, you will return to the monster you were fighting before.\nIf you manage to kill the monster you are fighting with, and you have already fought with all monsters that arrived before it, you will wait for the next monster to appear.\nIn the middle of the game, you took a break. You told your friend you had successfully defeated the KthK^{th}Kth monster before taking the break.\n\nYour friend wonders the number of different possible valid orders to defeat the remaining monsters. As the answer can be large, output it modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK — the total number of monsters, and the KthK^{th}Kth monster, which you have defeated before taking a break, respectively.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line number of possible valid orders of defeating the remaining monsters modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤5⋅1031 \\leq T \\leq 5 \\cdot 10^31≤T≤5⋅103",
      "1≤K≤N≤1031 \\leq K \\leq N \\leq 10^31≤K≤N≤103",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 5⋅1035 \\cdot 10^35⋅103."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n3 2\n420 69",
        "output": "5\n104751757",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The second monster has been defeated. So we will find all the possible cases of defeating the remaining monsters.\n\nCase 111: Monster 111 and 333 were already defeated. So the order of defeating the monsters becomes {}\\{\\}{}.\nCase 222: Monster 111 was defeated, but monster 333 didn't appear till now. So, the order of defeating the monsters becomes {3}\\{3\\}{3}.\nCase 333: Monster 333 was defeated, but monster 111 wasn't defeated. So the order of defeating the monsters becomes {1}\\{1\\}{1}.\nCase 444: Monster 111 wasn't defeated yet, but monster 333 didn't arrive yet. So the order of defeating the monsters becomes {1,3}\\{1,3\\}{1,3}.\nCase 555: Monster 111 wasn't defeated yet, but monster 333 did arrive. So the order of defeating the monsters becomes {3,1}\\{3,1\\}{3,1}.\n\nHence, there are a total of 555 possible ways."
      }
    ]
  },
